Technical
Firewall Configuration is Critical - Windows Firewall blocked SMB traffic initially; creating proper inbound rules was essential for log generation.
Field Mapping Matters - Kibana visualizations required the correct field names (source.ip, winlog.event_data.Image).
Protocol Compatibility - Hydra's SMB module is experimental; SMB2/SMB3 support requires explicit protocol flags.
Time Ranges are Important - Alert rules must use correct time windows to avoid missing events.

Operational
Document Everything - Detailed configuration files and commands save hours of debugging.
Test Continuously - Regular attack simulations validate detection capabilities.
Version Control - Save configuration files to GitHub for reproducibility.
